  <lesson id="les-l4-01-three-layers" title="Three layers for one campus" level="4" minutes="20" goal="A floor computer reaches the campus server through access, distribution and core"/>
  <step n="1" text="Read the canvas top to bottom: Core, then DistA and DistB, then AccessA and AccessB with the floor computers."/>
  <step n="2" text="On DistA create subinterfaces Gig0/2.10 and Gig0/2.20 with 172.17.10.1 and 172.17.20.1, and on DistB create Gig0/2.10 with 172.18.10.1. Every floor VLAN now has a gateway."/>
  <step n="3" text="On Core, DistA and DistB type router ospf 1, then announce every network each one touches with a network statement such as network 172.17.10.0 0.0.0.255 area 0." check="c1"/>
